W: 2. My minnie laid him at my back,
W: I trow he lay na lang at that,
W: But turn'd, and in a verra crack
W: Produc'd a dainty Davie.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: O, leeze me on your curly pow,
W: Bonnie Davie, dainty Davie;
W: Leeze me on your curly pow,
W: My ain dear dainty Davie.
W:
W: 3. Then in the field among the pease,
W: Behin' the house o' the Cherrytrees,
W: Again he wan atweesh my thies,
W: And splash, gaed out his gravy.
W: [Chorus]
W:
W: 4. But had I gold, or had I land,
W: I should be a' at his command;
W: I'll ne'er forget what he pat i' my hand,
W: It was a dainty Davie.
W: [Chorus]
W:
W:
W: Bowdlerized Lyrics:
W:
W: 1. (It was) in and through the window broads,
W: And all the tirliewirlies o'd;
W: The sweetest kiss that e'er I got
W: Was from my dainty Davie.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: O, leeze me on your curly pow,
W: Dainty Davie, dainty Davie.
W: Leeze me on your curly pow,
W: My ain dainty Davie.
W:
W: 2. It was down amang my daddy‘ pease,
W: And underneath the cherry trees;
W: O there he kist me as he pleased,
W: For he was mine ain dear Davie.
W:
W: 3. When he was chased by a dragoon,
W: Into my bed he was laid doon;
W: I thought him worthy o‘ his room,
W: And he's ay my dainty Davie.
